NAME
       dbgmon - the kernel debug monitor

SYNOPSIS
       dbgmon

DESCRIPTION
       Opens the console that shows the kernel log as it is written,
       coloured by severity: errors red, warnings yellow, successful
       steps green, debug grey. Ctrl-Alt-F2 reaches the same screen.

KEYS
       arrows, PgUp, PgDn   move through the log
       G, End               follow the newest line again
       /                    search; n repeats
       1 2 3 4 5            show only info, warnings, errors, ok, debug
       0                    show everything
       L                    change what the kernel records, which is
                            not the same as what is shown
       q, Esc               return

NOTES
       Scrolling never stops the log being collected. While you are
       reading, the status line counts the lines that have arrived.

SEE ALSO
       dmesg(1), drv(1), sysreport(1)
